      "id": 1,
      "text": "Jean Pierre Gueydan bought 40,000 acres in 1884 and, by 1896, turned a slice of that purchase into the town of Gueydan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17,
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gueydan%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Gueydan donated land and right‑of‑way to the Southern Pacific Railroad, sparking a branch line that linked the town to Midland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gueydan%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dubbed the Duck Capital of America, Gueydan hosts annual duck‑related festivals that draw visitors from across the state.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
